-## Gem Sniping
+**Spy history** is exclusive to this tab. It contains location/camera area,
+last clear empty check, first and last sighting, appearance window, first
+missing check, distinct runs seen and the original screenshot link. The check
+log retains each visit as present, empty or unclear; only its latest 1,000 rows
+are displayed, while the database retains all visits. Camera coordinates and
+within-view gem positions are approximate, not verified gem tile coordinates.
+
+Two successful empty observations in separate runs confirm an absence. Retries
+or overlapping views in one run cannot provide both confirmations. Loading,
+blank/changing scenes, unconfirmed candidates, locked views and capture failures
+are unclear, not empty. Persistent matching uses approximate positions with a
+small tolerance, including overlapping camera views. A visually identical gem
+collected and replaced between visits cannot be distinguished reliably.
+
+**Hourly history** groups new encounters by local date and the hour of their
+first confirmed sighting. A gem remaining into later hours is not counted again.
+UTC offsets distinguish repeated clock hours at daylight-saving changes. Counts
+are observed new encounters, not inferred actual spawn-hour totals.
+
+**Timing patterns** compares appearance windows by camera area and minutes of
+the hour, with supporting-window counts and median observed gaps. It needs at
+least three usable windows across two hours before showing candidate minute
+ranges. Windows remain observation bounds; they are not midpoint guesses or
+proof of a spawn schedule. Unknown first appearances and windows lasting an
+hour or more cannot identify a minute of the hour. Other players and missed
+appearances can affect the observed gaps.
+
+Capture/alignment failures release the button, retain state and retry with a
+short increasing delay. After two failed attempts, the point is recorded as
+unclear and the next selected-route point is attempted using fresh recognition.
+It is revisited on the next run. No blind reverse drags or guessed location
+clicks are used. Storage/setup errors are reported rather than silently losing
+data. This handles worker errors, not a hung or terminated Windows process.
+Original screenshots already written before a crash are recovered on startup;
+a later image is never substituted as the original first-sighting photo.
+
